== Introduction
<introduction>
Continuing the #strong[method of Hajj], this lesson covers the
#strong[8th of Dhū al-Ḥijjah (Yawm al-Tarwiyah)] at #strong[Minā], the
move to #strong[ʿArafāt] on the #strong[9th], the #strong[Wuqūf (وقوف)]
\[standing\] and its permitted area, the #strong[Ghusl] of ʿArafah, the
two #strong[Khuṭbahs], and --- in detail --- the #strong[Ḥanafī
jurisprudence of combining Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr (Jamʿ bayn al-Ṣalātayn)] at
ʿArafāt: its conditions, the congregation requirement, and the rulings
for resident vs.~traveller imams.

#horizontalrule

== Part 1 --- The 8th of Dhū al-Ḥijjah (Yawm al-Tarwiyah): Minā
<part-1-the-8th-of-dhu-al-hijjah-yawm-al-tarwiyah-mina>
- #strong[Movement:] On the #strong[8th (Yawm al-Tarwiyah / يوم
  التروية)], pilgrims move to #strong[Minā (منى)].
- #strong[The five prayers at Minā (Sunnah):] the pilgrim performs
  #strong[five prayers] there --- #strong[Ẓuhr, ʿAṣr, Maghrib, ʿIshā'],
  and the #strong[Fajr of the 9th] --- each #strong[at its own
  prescribed time] (not combined).
- #strong[Historical basis:] this follows the example of #strong[Ibrāhīm
  عليه السلام], whom #strong[Jibrā'īl عليه السلام] led in these five
  prayers at Minā after taking him there on the Day of Tarwiyah.

#horizontalrule

== Part 2 --- The 9th of Dhū al-Ḥijjah: Moving to ʿArafāt
<part-2-the-9th-of-dhu-al-hijjah-moving-to-arafat>
- #strong[Departure:] after the #strong[Fajr] prayer at Minā on the
  #strong[9th], the pilgrim waits until #strong[sunrise], then proceeds
  to #strong[ʿArafāt (عرفات)].
- #strong[Where to stand (Wuqūf):] a pilgrim may stand #strong[anywhere
  within the boundaries of ʿArafāt except Wādī ʿUranah (وادي عُرَنة)] ---
  the Valley of ʿUranah.

#quote(block: true)[
#strong[«عَرَفَاتُ كُلُّهَا مَوْقِفٌ، وَارْتَفِعُوا عَنْ بَطْنِ عُرَنَةَ»]

#emph["All of ʿArafāt is a place of standing, but keep away from the
bottom of ʿUranah."]

#strong[Ref:] Sunan Ibn Mājah, 3012 (also narrated in Abū Dāwūd).
]

- #strong[Ghusl of ʿArafah:] it is #strong[Mustaḥabb (recommended)] to
  make #strong[ghusl] on the day of ʿArafah --- for #strong[cleanliness]
  and to improve the atmosphere of the massive gathering, similar to the
  ghusl for #strong[Jumuʿah] or #strong[ʿĪd].

#horizontalrule

== Part 3 --- The Khuṭbah and Adhān
<part-3-the-khu-bah-and-adhan>
- #strong[Timing:] once the sun begins to decline (#strong[Zawāl /
  زوال]), the imam delivers #strong[two khuṭbahs] from the
  #strong[minbar].
- #strong[Purpose:] the primary aim is to #strong[teach the pilgrims the
  manāsik (مناسك)] \[rituals\] of Hajj.
- #strong[Sequence (preferred view):] the imam #strong[ascends the
  minbar first], and the #strong[adhān] is called while he is upon it.
- #strong[Its status --- Sunnah (not a condition of the prayer):] unlike
  the #strong[Jumuʿah] khuṭbah --- which is #strong[farḍ] for the
  validity of the prayer --- the #strong[ʿArafah khuṭbah is Sunnah]. The
  #strong[Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr remain valid] even if the khuṭbah is not
  delivered, though #strong[omitting it without reason is wrong], as it
  opposes the Prophet's ﷺ Sunnah.
- #strong[Content:] the sermon should #strong[begin with the Takbīr] and
  include teaching the specific rulings of Hajj.

#quote(block: true)[
#strong[«اللهُ أَكْبَرُ اللهُ أَكْبَرُ لَا إِلَهَ إِلَّا اللهُ وَاللهُ أَكْبَرُ اللهُ أَكْبَرُ وَلِلَّهِ
الْحَمْدُ»]

#emph["Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest; there is no deity
but Allah; Allah is the Greatest, Allah is the Greatest, and to Allah
belongs all praise."]
]

#horizontalrule

== Part 4 --- Combining Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr (Jamʿ bayn al-Ṣalātayn)
<part-4-combining-uhr-and-asr-jam-bayn-al-salatayn>
At ʿArafāt, #strong[Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr] are performed together #strong[in the
time of Ẓuhr] (#strong[Jamʿ Taqdīm / جمع تقديم]).

#strong[Procedure:]

- #strong[One adhān] for both prayers.
- #strong[Two separate iqāmahs] (one for Ẓuhr, one for ʿAṣr).
- #strong[No Sunnah or Nawāfil] are prayed #strong[between] the two farḍ
  prayers --- to avoid any break (faṣl). If a #strong[significant break]
  occurs, the Sunnah of combining is missed, and the default (a
  #strong[separate adhān] for each prayer) would technically apply.

#strong[Recitation style:] performed #strong[silently (sirrī)], exactly
like ordinary Ẓuhr and ʿAṣr --- #strong[not] aloud like Jumuʿah or ʿĪd
--- because the primary purpose of the ʿArafāt gathering is
#strong[Duʿā' and Wuqūf], not the prayer itself.

#horizontalrule

== Part 5 --- Ḥanafī Jurisprudence of the Combined Prayer
<part-5-hanafi-jurisprudence-of-the-combined-prayer>
The Ḥanafī school treats this combining as an #strong[exceptional case],
established #strong[strictly on the Prophet's ﷺ practice].

=== Conditions for combining
<conditions-for-combining>
+ #strong[Order:] #strong[Ẓuhr must be performed first], then
  #strong[ʿAṣr].
+ #strong[A valid Ẓuhr first:] the ʿAṣr must follow a #strong[valid
  Ẓuhr] --- one performed #strong[after the time of Zawāl has genuinely
  entered].

=== The congregation (jamāʿah) requirement
<the-congregation-jamaah-requirement>
According to the Ḥanafīs, this combination is #strong[only for those
praying with the imam] in the main congregation.

#figure(
  align(center)[#table(
    columns: (57.89%, 42.11%),
    align: (auto,auto,),
    table.header([Situation], [Ruling],),
    table.hline(),
    [#strong[Praying with the imam] (main jamāʿah)], [May
    #strong[combine] Ẓuhr & ʿAṣr],
    [#strong[Praying alone] (in one's tent or elsewhere)], [Must pray
    #strong[each at its own time] --- Ẓuhr at Ẓuhr time, ʿAṣr at ʿAṣr
